---
description: Architecture and permission rules for Chrome extension application code.
globs: ["apps/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,json,html,css}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Before editing an app, read its `docs/SPEC.md`, `docs/PERMISSIONS.md`, and `docs/QA.md`.

- Keep entrypoints thin; move reusable behavior into `lib/`.
- Background/service-worker code must survive suspension and reconstruct durable state from storage.
- Use typed messages with runtime validation at trust boundaries.
- Keep host-site selectors and undocumented API assumptions under `lib/adapters/<site>/`.
- Prefer `activeTab` and optional permissions over broad host access.
- Never add `<all_urls>` for convenience.
- Any new permission or host permission requires a matching update to `docs/PERMISSIONS.md`.
- Keep generated output out of source control.
- Do not introduce a UI framework unless the app complexity justifies it in the SPEC.
